# Single-phase pole-mount: 50 kVA, 7200/12470Y - 120/240 V, center-tapped secondary,
# one primary bushing (H1; H2 is internal, tied to the grounded tank).
# X2 is bonded to the tank (ground symbol on the middle secondary terminal; no
# attribute for it on a lug).
# Polarity: additive (single-phase, 200 kVA or less, 8660 V or less; IEEE C57.12.00).
# Polarity moves X1/X3 on the tank, not the model.
# Rating: IEEE C57.12.00-2021 Table 7 nameplate marking.
# Source: SRP Overhead Distribution Construction Standards, pages 7-33-1, 7-35-1,
# https://www.srpnet.com/v3/assets/bltefc1fc708dcc94e7/bltac008ac0402d979e/overhead-distribution-construction-standards.pdf
#
# The template is the tank only: lugs, windings and impedances. Each lug's
# sequenceNumber is the conductor it lands on, in terminal order: end 1 (H1, H2),
# then end 2 (X1 = s1, X3 = s2, X2 = N). An instance's TransformerPhaseEnds carry the
# same numbers and the real phases, so the same tank goes phase to neutral (7-33-1)
# or phase to phase (7-34-1). In a bank (7-35-1) each tank position has its own
# configuration, numbered over the bank: see bank_oyod_50_50_7200_12470y.cimtbl.
#
# Impedance and losses are illustrative (typical of a DOE 2016 50 kVA unit:
# 99.11 % at half load), not from a datasheet.

Profile = cim18v17

Object TransformerTankConfiguration: mRID=xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing, name=polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing, percentImpedance=2.0, noLoadLoss (W)=90, loadLoss (W)=540

# Bushing/lug designations per IEEE C57.12.70-2020, before the windings that name them.
Table TransformerLug: mRID, designation, sequenceNumber, TankConfiguration=xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing
    xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_lug_h1, H1, 1
    xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_lug_x1, X1, 2
    xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_lug_x3, X3, 3
    xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_lug_x2, X2, 4

# ratedU: the phase-to-phase designation (7200/12470Y -> 12470; 120/240 -> 240).
# ratedS: per phase on the split-phase secondary (each half 25 kVA).
# baseU: the coil voltage. baseS: the tank kVA, the base for all three coils.
# From = the polarity end: H1->H2, X1->X2, X2->X3 (OpenDSS s1->N, N->s2).
# H2 has no lug: the primary coil ends inside, on the grounded tank.
Table TransformerWinding: mRID, ratedU (V), baseU (V), ratedS (kVA), baseS (kVA), FromTransformerLug, ToTransformerLug, TankConfiguration=xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing
    xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_wdg_h1h2, 12470, 7200, 50, 50, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_lug_h1, 
    xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_wdg_x1x2, 240, 120, 25, 50, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_lug_x1, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_lug_x2
    xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_wdg_x2x3, 240, 120, 25, 50, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_lug_x2, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_lug_x3

# quality = inferred: half-winding impedances are not on the nameplate, so they come
# from the Hopkinson (1976) interlaced secondary model (Kersting Fig. 4.8), as in
# padmount_1ph_250kva.cimtbl. Full-winding impedance from the configuration:
#   R = loadLoss / ratedS = 540 / 50000 = 1.08 %
#   X = sqrt(percentImpedance^2 - R^2) = sqrt(2.0^2 - 1.08^2) = 1.6833 %
#   H - X1X2 = H - X2X3 = 1.5R + j1.2X  (OpenDSS Xhl, Xht)
#   X1X2 - X2X3         = 2.0R + j0.8X  (OpenDSS Xlt)
Table TransformerMeshImpedance: mRID, FromWinding, ToWinding, r (percent), x (percent)
    xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_mesh_h_x1x2, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_wdg_h1h2, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_wdg_x1x2, 1.62, 2.0200
    xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_mesh_h_x2x3, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_wdg_h1h2, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_wdg_x2x3, 1.62, 2.0200
    xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_mesh_x1x2_x2x3, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_wdg_x1x2, xc_polemount_1ph_50kva_7200_12470y_1bushing_wdg_x2x3, 2.16, 1.3467
